{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","record":{"id":"circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","kind":"claim","label":"Positive-temperature rooted output and clipping","status":"unverified","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:680–737; eq:classical-eams-vector, eq:clipped-classical-vector","statement":"For each fixed finite discretization, apply the smooth strong-limit lemma to the EAMS recursion to obtain a rooted z_δ with the scalar law Z_δ and rooted energy equal to its corrected edge sum. Since |m(T,X_T)|≤1, the scalar coupling yields ‖z_δ−clip(z_δ)‖≤C√δ, and root-shift continuity controls the energy loss. β₀, T and then δ are chosen to make the clipped rooted output arbitrarily near P_*.","assumption_ids":["circuit.positive_input"],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-rooted-clipping"],"boundary":"Scalar clipping uses the matching law only after the energy of z_δ has been identified by strong rooted convergence and occupation control. All choices remain finite."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/2f85413164f06365ea0d825befee447650da71d54080d5dd65e78a708891c560","roles":["mapped_claim"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/alternative-assembly","anchor":"alternative-assembly","mapping_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:c4249feffa26e48c24c5690f73e0de4886e40504c8c5c0e6dcb22ec94ea334da/papers/long.md/sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/passages/alternative-assembly","anchor":"alternative-assembly","mapping_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\nAfter clipping and bounded approximation, the result enters the same\nsynthesis and seed-removal route as the primary construction. Its source\ndependencies and fixed-temperature choice of parameters remain separate\nfrom the retained zero-temperature formal interfaces.\n[OpenAI (2026b), Appendix A][q-positive].\n\n<a id=\"temperature-route-comparison\"></a>\n\n### 11.1.1 Where the temperature routes meet\n\nBoth routes produce a bounded finite classical calculation whose rooted\nenergy is close to $P_*$. They reach that common input by different\ntheorems and different finite approximations.\n\n**Variational input and support.** The zero-temperature route fixes an\nattained minimizer $\\gamma\\in\\mathcal U$ with terminal value $|x|$ and\nuses full relative Stieltjes support on $[0,1)$. The positive-temperature\nroute fixes a finite $\\beta_0>1$ and its Parisi probability measure, with\nterminal value $\\beta_0^{-1}\\log(2\\cosh\\beta_0x)$; it uses Lopatto's\ninterval-support result on $[0,q_{\\beta_0}]$.\n\n**Scalar error.** Before discretization, the zero-temperature loss is at\nmost $1-T$ for $T<1$. The positive-temperature loss is at most\n$$\n(1/4+\\log2)/\\beta_0+(q_{\\beta_0}-T),\\qquad T<q_{\\beta_0}.\n$$\n\n**Finite energy.** In the zero-temperature route, a first-chaos projection\nidentifies the explicit Gaussian coefficient sum with\n$\\operatorname{Re}\\langle F_N,\\mathsf L F_N\\rangle$. The alternative\nroute first calculates finite-degree messages and edge energy, then uses\na rooted norm and occupation argument.\n\n**Order of approximation.** At zero temperature, fix $T$ before refining\nthe scalar mesh, and choose a finite mesh before regularization and synthesis.\nAt positive temperature, fix $\\beta_0,T,\\delta,L$ for the message degree\nlimit, then refine $\\delta$ at fixed $\\beta_0,T$.\n\nBoth routes then use the same bounded approximation, exclusions, seeded\nsynthesis, seed removal and fixed-word transfer. The quantum construction\nis shared; its classical input has been supplied independently.\n\nHere the displayed positive-temperature estimate is exactly the one\nderived above, rather than an assertion of convergence of zero-temperature\nsupports. One can choose $\\beta_0$ and $T$ finitely for the required\nerror and then stop. The later circuit argument needs that finite\nchoice; it never asks for a joint limit of the temperature, message\nmesh, graph degree and circuit depth. [OpenAI (2026b), Appendix A,\nProposition “The independent positive-temperature construction”][q-positive];\n[§6][q-assembly].\n","span":{"start_byte":216790,"end_byte":219297,"start_line":4687,"end_line":4737},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=alternative-assembly","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=long&passage=alternative-assembly"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=circuit.positive_rooted_clipping&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=circuit.positive_rooted_clipping&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=circuit.positive_rooted_clipping&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=circuit.positive_rooted_clipping&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:97c6d3ef9894eb87ab4303c2ccacbad11b6abed463126bee527b6c207c958373","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_input","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_positive%22%2C%22circuit.positive_rooted_clipping%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.classical_positive","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","derived":false,"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_positive%22%2C%22circuit.positive_rooted_clipping%22%2C%22supports%22%5D"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_rooted_clipping%22%2C%22circuit.classical_strong_limit%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_rooted_clipping","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.classical_strong_limit","kind":"supports","semantic_class":"curated_argument_suppor